# .docs-allowlist: exceptions for scripts/check-docs.sh.
#
# One entry per line; '#' starts a comment, blank lines are ignored.
#   <glob>        skip a whole file for every rule (bash glob, '*' also
#                 matches '/'), e.g.  docs/history/*
#   <path>:<line> skip one finding: for comment-block, any line inside the
#                 block; for md-link and docs-ref, the line of the link.
# Add an entry only with a reason in a comment above it (e.g. a vendored
# file, or a history doc that must quote an old path verbatim).
